r b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1206268#post1206268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, those are good reasons. Now i am picturing the PI running in to help the Sidhe after he or she gets caught by a group of thugs, only to find that he or she already whomped them. Another idea i had is to make his partner either a Native American or Hawaiian Gallian. How could that work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally they are better off in more natural setups but really that and their totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:02:48-07:00","id":1206419,"title":"","content":"Good point. With a Pooka, i can see shifting shape into animals and spying on people. But, the problem is that Pooka's almost always lie so, you can see the problem there. Not to sure how a Eshu could make a good partner since they tend to like to wander instead of staying in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:30:40-07:00","id":1206462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1206419#post1206419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. With a Pooka, i can see shifting shape into animals and spying on people. But, the problem is that Pooka's almost always lie so, you can see the problem there. Not to sure how a Eshu could make a good partner since they tend to like to wander instead of staying in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everyone lies. No really, basic politeness is a countless series of lies. Yes the Pooka is going to be abit more tricky about it.. but they can give you information they just have theirown ways. And nothing says and Eshu aren't any more driven to wander than Gangrel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T11:29:42-07:00","id":1206537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1206462#post1206462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everyone lies. No really, basic politeness is a countless series of lies. Yes the Pooka is going to be abit more tricky about it.. but they can give you information they just have theirown ways. And nothing says and Eshu aren't any more driven to wander than Gangrel</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Eshu would be interesting partner for him to have. I wonder what a Eshu could do to help solve mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T13:52:26-07:00","id":1206634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1206537#post1206537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Eshu would be interesting partner for him to have. I wonder what a Eshu could do to help solve mysteries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solve it in the most interesting way possible!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T14:28:56-07:00","id":1206661,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the Eshu Birthrights pretty much insures that they'll find the right clues at the right time. (And if taken to farcical levels, will have them tripping over dead bodies and other case-starters on the way to work every morning.)<br /> <br /> As for Boggins in danger, given how useful the first two levels of Primal are for a &quot;house spirit&quot; type, I have frequently found it not uncommon for more experienced Boggin NPCs to end up knowing Oakenshield and Holly Strike as well. And if all else fails, Wayfare is useful for running away. (I also long ago home ruled that Boggins have their own version of Sovereign - Sanctuary - that applies to households, places of commerce, religious sites and other areas of community importance.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T15:24:32-07:00","id":1206682,"title":"","content":"Now i am picturing a Eshu telling a story about the time how he and his mortal partner busted a counterfeit watch ring after the Eshu buys a fake Swiss watch. Now i am wondering how Inanimae could work as partners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 04-13-2018, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T05:52:02-07:00","id":1206860,"title":"","content":"I am wondering how solving mysteries and busting criminals could possibly generate Glamour. Because, if it can, that would be a great reason for a Changeling to persue this career in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:59:58-07:00","id":1206925,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of the dwarf from Dragon Age who writes pulp noir detective novels.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for Inanimae, that would be ... odd. I think the biggest hurdle is finding a suitable anchor. Mannikins would be easiest (Detective Barbie?), especially given the long running genre tropre of human detective with robot partner. I now have this image of the archetypical Gal Friday who is secretly a bonzai tree, and subtly manipulates people -including her boss - into growing in acertain way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:15:32-07:00","id":1206977,"title":"","content":"I figured that a Manakin and Dryad would be the easiest to justify. Because, Glomes and the inanimae of fire, air and water would be hard to justify, due to how hard it would be to have stone, air or water anchors in a PI's office. Then again, a image of a Gloam punching out a heavily tatooed guy in a tank top is currently playing in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T14:04:32-07:00","id":1207008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1206977#post1206977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured that a Manakin and Dryad would be the easiest to justify. Because, Glomes and the inanimae of fire, air and water would be hard to justify, due to how hard it would be to have stone, air or water anchors in a PI's office. Then again, a image of a Gloam punching out a heavily tatooed guy in a tank top is currently playing in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anchor no more has to be in the office than a changelings freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:54:23-07:00","id":1207040,"title":"","content":"For Glomes? An antique stone carving of a falcon originally crafted by the Knights Hospitaller. Or a stone bust of Humphrey Bogart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:40:03-07:00","id":1207127,"title":"","content":"I like the bust of Humphrey Boggart idea. The wind Inanimae anchor could be either a AC or a flute. Not to sure about the flame or water one, unless their Anchors are in a nearby freehold.<br /> <br /> I wondet why a Inanimae would be interested in working with a meat investigator?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:56:36-07:00","id":1207136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1207127#post1207127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the bust of Humphrey Boggart idea. The wind Inanimae anchor could be either a AC or a flute. Not to sure about the flame or water one, unless their Anchors are in a nearby freehold.<br /> <br /> I wondet why a Inanimae would be interested in working with a meat investigator?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They don't have to keep their anchor there though for fire, fireplaces, stoves, furnaces, forges, lamps. For water Fountains<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T22:46:25-07:00","id":1207172,"title":"","content":"An antique Zippo lighter owned by a 40s or 50s gumshoe. Or a hip flask, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T08:43:39-07:00","id":1207286,"title":"","content":"Good suggestions for the anchors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T13:29:49-07:00","id":1210572,"title":"","content":"Look at me, a necromancer prodigal!<br /> <br /> I did a quick and dirty list of the Kiths and Gallain, not including Hsien, Inanimae, Thallain, or other Changeling types. All* of them provided something useful to a detective/PI chronicle, even if it was their frailty. Several were good as muscle, a couple nice for picking up secrets, a fair majority were socially apt that could glean some measure of information in varying sizes of groups. To say any of the base thirteen kiths is not good in this means someone isn't using some available ability, birthright, or frailty to their best ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *The exception here is the Mer, not because they don't have an applicable effect somewhere in their birthrights and frailties, but simply because of their lack of contact with humans. That isolationist ideology of theirs makes them difficult to <i>easily</i> integrate them into such a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:29:24-07:00","id":1212466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1205663-which-kith-would-make-a-good-pi-partnet?p=1206860#post1206860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wondering how solving mysteries and busting criminals could possibly generate Glamour. Because, if it can, that would be a great reason for a Changeling to persue this career in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Musing table on page 261 of C20:<br /> <br /> Create Hope: &quot;I know everything seems lost, but hang in there. I've seen more hopeless cases turn out alright.&quot;<br /> <br /> Create Love: Simple enough, keep the client obsessing over the person you're rescuing until they can't think of anything else.<br /> <br /> Help Those In Need: &quot;Ah, keep it. Putting this one away will be good for everyone.&quot;<br /> <br /> Foster Trust: &quot;I know you're scared, but I need you to tell me everything if I'm going to find your boy. Take your time.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}